Z||000000||horseman||12-06-2000||01:57 AM||||Has anyone tried an adjustable timing controller(MSD) on their cars? Paul Kadis says it almost feels like applying boost if you use it correctly. He also states that it might improve on economy. He thinks that other than a perf. camshaft that this is the best mod. for a 2.5 duke. Any ideas or opinions on this?<P>Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||12-06-2000||10:36 AM||||an RPM activated switch to trigger a retard... had it on my Nitrous car but it was part of the NOS controller not the MSD.. the MSD sure would look and i'm sure work nicer.. the Crane HI-6TR does this! all in one box. the MSD you have to get a retard box or a 6BTM and lie to it about boost. huumm.. not a bad idea.. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-06-2000||09:21 PM||||It's been my experience that you want to advance timing on a normally aspireated engine to gain power. The trick is figuring how far to advance and not cook the engine.<P>You have to be really carefull playing with ignition timing. You can blow holes in pistons if you mess up. If you do this then do it in very small steps. If you introduce knock/ping then back it off ASAP. Pull over to the side of the road if you have to. don't keep driving.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-06-2000).]||||reg||1
